{"title":"2003 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(semi-bash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (semi-bash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> be a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rhombus\" title=\"Rhombus\">rhombus</a> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/8/b48400ad142564047239528eb768167e1024f04c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7cbfe78f62f7fac766af327f1cfa1c237639ab6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = 30$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the feet of the perpendiculars from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" />, respectively. Which of the following is closest to the minimum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />?\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/2/c22d4d20155faaf8bd0cf51f26a5795d14b32322.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(200); defaultpen(0.6); pair O = (15*15/17,8*15/17), C = (17,0), D = (0,0), P = (25.6,19.2), Q = (25.6, 18.5); pair A = 2*O-C, B = 2*O-D; pair P = (A+O)/2, Q=(B+O)/2, N=(A+B)/2; draw(A--B--C--D--cycle); draw(A--O--B--O--C--O--D); draw(P--N--Q); label(&quot;\\(A\\)&quot;,A,WNW); label(&quot;\\(B\\)&quot;,B,ESE); label(&quot;\\(C\\)&quot;,C,ESE); label(&quot;\\(D\\)&quot;,D,SW); label(&quot;\\(P\\)&quot;,P,SSW); label(&quot;\\(Q\\)&quot;,Q,SSE); label(&quot;\\(N\\)&quot;,N,NNE); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"195\" /></center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d7f359e37d7f1b581971bdbf48f6b4c90dda72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ 6.5 \\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 6.75  \\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ 7 \\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ 7.25 \\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ 7.5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"416\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rhombus, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Perpendicular_bisector\" title=\"Perpendicular bisector\">perpendicular bisectors</a>. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/6/58656922d810aa5ccda634029c19a7b65a14fbb7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POQ = 90^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"104\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/6/3a677ba660e288a7c378ac7a3fbd5764df2e60a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OPNQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"58\" height=\"16\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Rectangle\" title=\"Rectangle\">rectangle</a>. Since the diagonals of a rectangle are of equal length, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916523eac03a3253e7f2a729252e1b5beb1eb68b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ = ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"83\" height=\"16\" />, so we want to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/b/afb3aa28627d70a5c4421063effb76bd2241a7e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ON$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"14\" />. It follows that we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/4/2c4ba875c55cd8b676dd6a55e8a05378708fa1b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ON \\perp AB$\" width=\"82\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Finding the area in two different ways,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/1/371850bee3734501625e187c81316234c3199ad1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{2}   AO \\cdot BO = 60 = \\frac{1}{2} ON \\cdot AB = \\frac{\\sqrt{8^2 + 15^2}}{2} \\cdot ON \\Longrightarrow ON = \\frac{120}{17} \\approx 7.06 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{(C)}\\]\" width=\"597\" height=\"41\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28semi-bash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(semi-bash)\">Solution 2 (semi-bash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (semi-bash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> is a rhombus, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39facf4ed73f7886f111ff2466878db18e5d8958.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC} \\perp \\overline{BD}$\" width=\"82\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/8/fe844229e7f270eef5958c65a606618f98e50a5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = CE = \\dfrac{AC}{2} = 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"170\" height=\"38\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/6/496d5524a239817038e678993f5b6ef788eaffc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{NQ} \\perp \\overline{BD}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"19\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d669300df0a9d8c577f1a415e07c7190f2f9756.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{NQ} \\parallel \\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fcc539094bd95d41a6efd586284e39c7158a1da.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BNQ} \\sim \\triangle{BAE} \\sim \\triangle{NAP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"229\" height=\"17\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/6/f46fad6ccc2f1bfa1d7c3e0bb437cd6ea3464a05.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\dfrac{NP}{AP} = \\dfrac{NP}{8 - NQ} = \\dfrac{BE}{AE} = \\dfrac{15}{8} \\Rightarrow NP = 15 - \\dfrac{15}{8} NQ.\\]\" width=\"407\" height=\"40\" /> By Pythagorean Theorem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/d/27df7eda9cf54b219ace5f34ca4a328e8eda5db0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PQ^2 = NQ^2 + NP^2 = NQ^2 + \\left(15 - \\dfrac{15}{8} NQ \\right)^2 = \\dfrac{289}{64} NQ^2 - \\dfrac{225}{4} NQ + 225.\\]\" width=\"569\" height=\"46\" /> The minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3d766a62ed39a0dc746377fc1d9342c8412e82.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"18\" /> would give the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />, so we take the derivative (or use vertex form) to find that the minimum occurs when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a495faf7845aa660a2180d5d2700a2ab80c08f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$NQ = \\dfrac{225 \\cdot 8}{289}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"106\" height=\"37\" /> which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb466fc0b806fa56901b7903813ee48e2e3a8a1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ^2 = \\dfrac{225 \\cdot 64}{289}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />. Hence, the minimum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/b/7ab17967324fc2b12349c0610c6c256f4c829162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/8/f68f2eef8e7b6e1b49df733aaf3b8c888377a55e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{\\dfrac{225 \\cdot 64}{289}} = \\dfrac{120}{17}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -14px\" width=\"134\" height=\"43\" />, which is closest to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/e/d/fed62fc053e832bf0ac53cad66d9683f21391b4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{\\textbf{C}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>-MP8148\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the intersection <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/7/4373e7b4be983c0315e82e1fda1df66ed34dd7fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BD}$\" width=\"30\" height=\"15\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/0/710fb5fa3adedd7a16739e543d846747adbe05b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/2/63238c07401c9eaa10f1e42c6118d81e164164a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PE}=y \\implies \\overline{AP}=8-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/c/ddcd139d0c4c608ec6e48054296940def987355e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{EQ}=x \\implies \\overline {QB}=15-x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"224\" height=\"21\" /> Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/9/3798f516d5b371fed449b040ad794593758d3ad9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle NQB \\sim \\triangle APN,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"153\" height=\"18\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/4/654891914eb6e1b97f00a629dc088d36766742bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{8-y}{x}=\\frac{y}{15-x} \\implies 120=15y+8x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"301\" height=\"40\" /> We want to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/a/42a05659c4c5264805a43c7c2ed78ab9b5ef8742.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{PQ}=\\sqrt{x^2+y^2}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"135\" height=\"24\" /> By Cauchy, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/d/50d3540679a5992874b7284b9fd0e599d272a5b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17^2(x^2+y^2)=(x^2+y^2)(8^2+15^2) \\ge (8x+15y)^2=120^2 \\implies \\sqrt{x^2+y^2} \\ge \\frac{120}{17} \\approx 7.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"665\" height=\"38\" /> So, choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f58d2efaaa17d28cec9dd927d78708a63b43e24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{C}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"24\" /> is closest to the minimum.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2003_AMC_12B\" title=\"2003 AMC 12B\">2003 AMC 12B</a></b> (<